<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22141" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn -aequābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>uneven</i>, <i>unequal</i>
			(rare, but good prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campester locus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 6, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					35, 28, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venarum inaequabili percussu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 51, 52, § 171</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haec inaequabili varietate distinguimus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Part. Or. 4, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			number, <i>disproportionate</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 2, 4, 22</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnaequābĭlĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>unevenly</i>, <i>unequally</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maturescunt ova,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 9, 8</span></i>
			 Schneider: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rexit provinciam (with varie),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Galb. 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gessit censuram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Claud. 16</span></i>
			.</div>
